  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#following-hyperlinks\r\n\r\n> Let resource be a new request whose url is URL and whose referrer policy is the current state of subject's referrerpolicy content attribute\\.\r\n\r\nThere should be an additional step which sets the referrer policy of _resource_ to \"no-referrer\" if _subject_'s link types include noreferrer.\r\n\r\nThen, https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#link-type-noreferrer should be updated, so that instead of the normative requirement\r\n\r\n> If a user agent follows a link defined by an a or area element that has the noreferrer keyword, the user agent must set their request's referrer to \"no-referrer\".\r\n\r\nit instead says something like \"This link type's affects on a or area elements is defined in the algorithm for following hyperlinks.\"",
